3. Required product credit

Every game or application distributed or made available to end users that
includes the Software or a modified version must display the following credit:

    Uses Unity Shop System by Mateusz Ciszek.

Place this credit in a reasonably accessible credits or About screen, or in
user-facing documentation distributed with the product. The credit must be
legible and accessible to end users; a source-code comment alone is insufficient.
This requirement applies to both free and commercial products. Private use
without distribution or availability to end users does not require product credit.

4. No sale as a reusable development product

You may not sell, license for a fee, or otherwise provide for payment access to
the Software, modified versions, or substantial portions of it as a standalone
or reusable development product. This includes asset packs, plugins, libraries,
templates, toolkits, and paid source-code packages, whether offered alone or
bundled with other development materials. Renaming, modifying, or repackaging
the Software does not remove this restriction.

This restriction does not prohibit selling or monetizing games or applications
that incorporate the Software for their end-user functionality, as permitted
in section 2. It also does not prohibit paid work integrating or customizing
the Software for such a game or application. A product marketed or supplied as
a means to obtain the Software for reuse in other projects remains subject to
the restriction, even if described as a game or application.

